Plain HTML: banner markup in every page (layout/partial), classic script at the end of <body>, CSS in the site stylesheet. No nonce exists on a static host: scripts/csp-hashes.mjs (headers recipe) adds the SRI hash of /consent.js to the tag and to the CSP, and 'strict-dynamic' trusts the Google tag this script creates, so do not host-allow Google in script-src. Put consent.js at the site root, not in a cached-forever hashed folder. List `consent` under essentialCookies and set consent.banner.acceptLabel/rejectLabel/reopenLabel to the three labels. Build with CSP_CONNECT_EXTRA="https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com" CSP_IMG_EXTRA="https://www.google-analytics.com" (beacons only).
