A static site has no server of its own, so this recipe is the CLIENT part only. The endpoint (serverless function or the project's API; the placeholder is https://example.com/api/contact) MUST implement: same-origin check on `Origin` (fallback `Sec-Fetch-Site`), 403 for cross-site; per-client rate limit answering 429 after N submissions; discard a submission whose honeypot field `website` is filled while answering the same success response; server-side validation and length limits; delivery to the real destination (email provider API, FORM_WEBHOOK_URL or database insert) with an ~8s timeout, answering 502/503 when delivery fails and 2xx/303 only after it succeeded; Turnstile verification is the alternative to the honeypot. Without JavaScript the form posts natively and the endpoint answers 303 to a thank-you page. If the endpoint is on another origin, build with CSP_CONNECT_EXTRA="https://example.com" CSP_FORM_EXTRA="https://example.com" (headers recipe) and enable CORS for your site's origin on the endpoint; a same-origin path such as /api/contact needs neither.
