robots.txt, sitemap.xml and the non-production noindex header are generated after the site build from DEPLOY_ENV (set it in the host's build environment: `production` only on the production deploy; Netlify deploy previews and branch deploys must not be `production`). It runs after csp-hashes.mjs because `_headers` carries X-Robots-Tag; if `_headers` is missing it appends the rule itself. The sitemap lists every built HTML page that is not noindex and not an error page, using the page's own `<link rel="canonical">` as the URL (so canonicals must be absolute https URLs on SITE_URL with one trailing-slash policy). Remove any hand-written robots.txt/sitemap.xml from the source folder. Needs SITE_URL=https://example.com in production. Edit the PRIVATE list to your real app/API paths (never asset, CSS or JS folders).
